 Implemtation :-
 ASAP :- Accelerated SAP
 
	ASAP (Accelerated SAP) is SAP's implementation methodology that provides a step-by-step approach, templates, tools, and
	best practices for implementing SAP solutions.
	
	There are 5 phases in the ASAP methodology:
      
	  1) Project Preparation
	  2) Business Blueprint
	  3) Realization
	  4) Final Preparation
	  5) Go-Live
	  6) Support
	
	1) Project Preparation :- 
		
		Project Scoping / Deliverables
		Project Deadline
		Number of business process go-live
		Number of modules 
		Interfacs list
		Resource Planning
		
	2) Business Blueprint
		
		Business WorkShopes
		AS-IS(Existing Business Process)
		To-Be(New Business Process)
		GAPS
		Business Signoff and Reviews
		
	3) Realization
		
		Standard Configurations
		Write FSD(Functional Specification Document) for development objects
		Testing
		TR(Transport Request) List
		Move changes to quality system
		
	4) Final Preparation
		
		Testing Internally
		User training
		UAT(User Acceptance Testing)
		Cutover activities
		Data migration
		
	5) Go-Live

		Issues and errors reporting
		defect resolution
		
	6) Support

		issues reporting
		issues resolution
		
		
