Purchase order :-
---------------
	A Purchse Order is an offical document sent by a buyer to vendor to purchase material or service , it contains details such as the material, quantity, 
	price, delivery date, payment terms and delivery location.
	
	create  --->  ME21N
	
	Standard document type ---> NB , FO
	
	Configurations :-
	
		document types 
		number ranges 
		item categories 
		account assignment 
		release strategy 
		Screen Layout
		output settings.
	
	Types of Purchase Orders:-
		
	Standard Purchase Order (NB):-
	-----------------------------
		A Standard Purchase Order is the most commonly used PO. It is created for the one-time procurement of materials or services from a vendor.

		Characteristics:-
			Used for one-time purchases.
			Can be created with or without a Purchase Requisition.
			Supports material and service procurement.
			Goods Receipt (GR) and Invoice Verification (IV) are generally required.
			
	Subcontracting Purchase Order (Item Category: L):-
	--------------------------------------------------
		A Subcontracting PO is used when a company sends raw materials or components to a vendor, who manufactures or assembles the finished 
		product and returns it.		
	

	Consignment Purchase Order (Item Category: K):-
	---------------------------------------------
		A Consignment PO is used when materials are stored at the company's premises but remain the property of the vendor until they are consumed.

		Characteristics:-
			Ownership remains with the vendor.
			Payment is made only after consumption.
			Inventory is available immediately.	
			
			
Service Purchase Order (Item Category: D):-
-----------------------------------------
    A Service Purchase Order is used for procuring services instead of physical materials.

	Characteristics:-
		Uses Item Category D.
		Services are recorded using a Service Entry Sheet (ML81N).
		Common for maintenance, consulting, security, and housekeeping.	

Framework Order (Item Category: B):-
-----------------------------------
	A Framework Order is used for recurring or low-value services where the exact quantity is not known.

	Characteristics:-
		Uses Item Category B (Limit).
		Defines an overall value limit and validity period.
		Suitable for miscellaneous services.	


Scheduling Arrangement:-
-----------------------
	A Scheduling Agreement (SA) is a long-term purchasing agreement between a company and a vendor in which the material, price, and 
	terms are fixed, but the delivery dates and quantities are scheduled over time instead of creating multiple Purchase Orders.	


		Create ---> ME31L
		
		
	Scheduling Agreement with Release Documentation :-
	-----------------------------------------------
		In this type, SAP creates release documents (forecast or JIT releases) from the scheduling agreement and sends them to the vendor.	
		
		
	Features:-
		Uses Forecast Delivery Schedules and/or JIT (Just-in-Time) Delivery Schedules.
		Release documents are generated and transmitted to the vendor.
		Commonly used in automotive and manufacturing industries.
		Suitable for frequent deliveries based on production planning.
		Vendor receives updated delivery schedules regularly.	
		
		
	Scheduling Agreement without Release Documentation:-
	--------------------------------------------------
	   (In this type, SAP does not generate release documents)

		The vendor delivers directly according to the schedule lines maintained in the scheduling agreement.

	Features:-
		No forecast or JIT releases.
		Delivery dates and quantities are maintained directly in the scheduling agreement.
		Simpler to manage.
		Suitable for businesses with stable delivery schedules.
		Vendor refers directly to the schedule lines.	









		
